{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 17, :comments ["And the sense of <b>pray forgive my sin</b> is by way of honor to Moses, for he is Elohim to Pharaoh (Exodus 7:1) and very great in the land of Egypt (Exodus 11:3). <b>And entreat YHWH your Elohim</b> — to both of them, for so Pharaoh says every time by way of rebuke, for Pharaoh knows that it is Moses who entreats, for so he said to him: \"Until when shall I entreat for you?\" (Exodus 8:8), \"And I shall entreat YHWH\" (Exodus 8:25), \"I shall spread my hands unto YHWH\" (Exodus 9:29) — for Moses would not speak in this case in plural language, so as not to bring forth a falsehood from his mouth."], :book :exodus, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 10, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:05:30.692880437Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}